# Nothing under runs/ is tracked.
#
# A run is the output of a tool on the NPU: the raw dumps (gigabytes) and the result.json
# beside them. Neither belongs in the repository:
#
#   * the dumps are reproducible from the tool that wrote them;
#   * result.json is not, on the machine that matters -- CI has no NPU, so a test that read
#     one was asserting what somebody once observed, not what the code does now. Those tests
#     are gone; the behaviour they guarded is pinned by the C++ unit tests instead
#     (src/test/buffer_range_test.cpp, diagnostic_range_test.cpp, prefill_route_reason_test.cpp,
#     layer_major_policy_test.cpp), which run on every runner.
#
# A tool still writes here so a person can inspect a run, and the reports quote a path when
# it matters. It is a scratch directory, not a fixture.
runs/
